
====================================================================================================
E. constants of S22 and the identity e^(-I) 3^(theta*/ln 2) = log_2 3 - 1
====================================================================================================
m = log_2 3 = 1.584963, p = log_3 2 = 0.630930, q = 1 - p = 0.369070, theta* = ln(2q) = -0.303621, I = theta* m - ln(m-1) = 0.054979
e^(-I) = 0.946505 (S22: 3^(h*-1) = 0.946505); theta*/ln 2 = -0.43803 (note: -0.438)
e^(-I) 3^(theta*/ln 2) = 0.584962500721156; log_2 3 - 1 = 0.584962500721156; difference -1.1e-16
algebra: 3^(theta*/ln 2) = e^(theta* ln 3/ln 2) = e^(theta* m); e^(-I) = e^(-theta* m) (m-1); product = m - 1.  The identity is the
         definition of I rewritten (I := theta* m - ln(m-1)); it holds for ANY theta*, not only the tilt -- it carries no information about the law.
3^(-1/2) = 0.577350; (m-1) = 0.584963; ratio 3^(-1/2)/(m-1) = 0.98699 -> margin 1.30% (note: 1.3%)
Chernoff extrapolation at u = 3^n: e^(-nI) 3^(n theta*/ln 2) = (m-1)^n = 0.5850^n; Parseval rms scale 3^(-n/2) = 0.5774^n
3^n (m-1)^(2n) = (1.0265)^n: a family of ~3^n units each of size (m-1)^n would carry a Fourier mass growing like 1.0265^n -- the note's 'Parseval forbids' reading (heuristic: the families u 2^j overlap)

