   T^2(1 + 4^j t) = 1 + 3 4^(j-1) t for j = 1..7, t = 1..199: True  (x = 1 mod 4: T(x) = (3x+1)/2 = 2 + 3 2^(2j-1) t even for j >= 1, T^2 = 1 + 3 4^(j-1) t; induction gives T^(2j)(1 + 4^j t) = 1 + 3^j t)
   chain 1 + 3^j 4^(m-j) -> 1 + 3^(j+1) 4^(m-j-1) under T^2 for m <= 11: True
